      "title": "More than 150,000 underwater explosives used to deter seals at Tasmanian salmon farms since 2016",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/22/underwater-explosives-used-to-deter-seals-at-tasmanian-salmon-farms-since-2016",
      "description": "<p>Salmon companies operating in Tasmanian marine areas deployed almost 1,800 explosives in first half of 2026, government figures reveal</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>More than 150,000 underwater explosives have been used to deter seals at Tasmanian salmon farms since 2016, according to new government data.</p><p>Department of Natural Resources and Environment (NRE Tas) data released last week <a href=\"https://nre.tas.gov.au/Documents/Wildlife%20interaction%20data%20reported%20by%20the%20salmonid%20aquaculture%20industry%20January%20-%20June%202026.pdf\">revealed</a> salmon companies directed almost 1,800 underwater explosives at seals at fish farms in the first half of 2026.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/22/underwater-explosives-used-to-deter-seals-at-tasmanian-salmon-farms-since-2016\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T15:00:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Discovery of new Australian stick insect species reveals case of mistaken identity",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/22/two-new-australian-stick-insect-species-found-queensland",
      "description": "<p>New study describes two species, <em>Anchiale robusta</em> and <em>Anchiale mabiensis</em>, both found in far north Queensland</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Two new large stick insect species have been identified by Australian researchers, in a discovery they say illustrates how little we still understand about insect diversity.</p><p>The two species, both found in far north Queensland, are described in a study published in <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/aen.70096\">Austral Entomology</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/22/two-new-australian-stick-insect-species-found-queensland\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T15:00:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Boy, 11, in serious condition after being shot in face and neck in Sydney home",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/boy-11-in-serious-condition-after-being-shot-in-face-and-neck-in-sydney-home-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Three 18-year-old men were arrested at the unit in Norwest, police said, but officers played down link to organised crime </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An 11-year-old boy has been taken to hospital in a serious condition after being shot in a home in Sydney’s north-west.</p><p>The child was receiving life-saving treatment in hospital on Monday night after suffering gunshot wounds to his face and neck, police said.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/boy-11-in-serious-condition-after-being-shot-in-face-and-neck-in-sydney-home-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T10:55:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Think Australia would be better off with less migration? The numbers tell a different story",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/australia-migration-ageing-population-labor-analysis-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>The population is ageing and we’re having fewer babies. Labor should keep that in mind as the migration debate rages</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-2026-deaths-outnumber-births-australia2060s\">intergenerational report</a> lays bare how today’s growing anti-migration rhetoric clashes with a future where we need to attract people from overseas to help grow the economy and pay for our ageing population.</p><p>The “replacement” fertility rate is 2.1 children per woman – this is the average number of births to keep the population steady without migration and we’ve been below this level for 50 years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/australia-migration-ageing-population-labor-analysis-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T09:35:08"
    }
  ]
